WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.200
Attention works on sets, so positions must be added.

2
00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:09.923
Lecture note 2 (01:12:46) observes that attention has no notion of space.

3
00:00:10.203 --> 00:00:27.163
Formally, self-attention without a mask is permutation equivariant: permute the input tokens and the outputs are permuted the same way, because every operation (the projections, the dot products, the softmax over keys, the weighted sum) treats positions symmetrically.

4
00:00:27.443 --> 00:00:42.589
Without some positional signal, “dog bites man” and “man bites dog” contain the same multiset of tokens and would get the same per-token representations (the causal mask breaks the symmetry only partially, by restricting who sees whom).

5
00:00:42.869 --> 00:00:58.421
The lecture’s fix, at 01:00:18, is a second embedding table indexed by position: the input to the first block is the token embedding plus a learned position embedding, a vector for each of the block_size positions.

6
00:00:58.701 --> 00:01:09.709
The original transformer paper used fixed sinusoidal encodings instead; many recent models use other schemes that inject relative position into the attention scores.

7
00:01:09.989 --> 00:01:15.131
The common point is that order is information the architecture doesn’t provide for free.

8
00:01:15.411 --> 00:01:28.381
One consequence is directly visible in your project: the position table has exactly block_size rows, so a model trained with context 64 has no representation at all for position 65.

9
00:01:28.661 --> 00:01:31.285
Context length is baked into the parameters.
